      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.08,
          "end": 2.41,
          "en": "Now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.41,
          "end": 4.73,
          "en": "What did we learn about objects and arrays?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.75,
          "end": 9.76,
          "en": "There's one common misconception I sometimes see in the Q&A section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.39,
          "end": 16.54,
          "en": "Please check out that video I linked earlier in this article where I talk about primitive and referenced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.54,
          "end": 20.02,
          "en": "types and JavaScript because that is a crucial concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.2,
          "end": 26.68,
          "en": "Objects and arrays are so called reference types and you'll learn all about that and what that is in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.68,
          "end": 27.37,
          "en": "the linked video.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.37,
          "end": 29.32,
          "en": "So I'm not going to re-explain it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.05,
          "end": 39.81,
          "en": "They are reference types and therefore when I store an array in a constant hobbies, I can still edit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 39.81,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "disarray without violating the restriction that constants must not change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 47.28,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "Let me prove that to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 49.9,
          "end": 57.46,
          "en": "If I comment that out and I add a new line here and I use another method to push method which allows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 57.46,
          "end": 60.15,
          "en": "me to add a new element to the existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 60.16,
          "end": 62.26,
          "en": "So this will not return a new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 62.29,
          "end": 64.15,
          "en": "It will add it to the existing array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 64.45,
          "end": 67.39,
          "en": "And here I will add programming.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 68.33,
          "end": 72.83,
          "en": "Now if I now console log hobbies after pushing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 73.59,
          "end": 75.81,
          "en": "And I run note pledges.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 76.35,
          "end": 77.94,
          "en": "You see, that is the output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 77.94,
          "end": 81.87,
          "en": "And we get no error about editing this constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 82.75,
          "end": 92.2,
          "en": "The reason for that is that reference types only store an address pointing at the place in memory where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 92.2,
          "end": 94.78,
          "en": "that array is stored and that pointer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 94.78,
          "end": 98.92,
          "en": "This address has not changed by us adding a new element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 99.16,
          "end": 106.21000000000001,
          "en": "So the thing stored in this constant is just this pointer, just this address, and this has not changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 106.21000000000001,
          "end": 109.57,
          "en": "Therefore our constant value has not changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 110.93,
          "end": 116.3,
          "en": "The thing it's pointing at has changed, but that totally does not matter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 116.63,
          "end": 121.4,
          "en": "And this is something you have to understand so that you don't wonder what's going on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 121.4,
          "end": 126.26,
          "en": "When we do edit in quotation marks a constant value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 126.29,
          "end": 129.5,
          "en": "We're not really editing the thing that is stored in a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 129.53,
          "end": 134.57,
          "en": "We're only editing the thing that constant thing is pointing at.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
